flow-regime-4e7283f1.conceptual_definition:
The formula presented, known as the Reynolds number (
Re
), is a dimensionless quantity crucial in fluid dynamics for predicting flow patterns in different fluid flow situations. It serves as a ratio comparing inertial forces to viscous forces within a fluid. Understanding the Reynolds number allows engineers and physicists to determine whether a fluid flow will be laminar (smooth and orderly) or turbulent (chaotic and irregular), which has significant implications for phenomena such as drag, heat transfer, and mixing.

